{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And Moses came.</b> It does not mention \"and he went down from the mountain,\" because there is no need." "The sense of \"and Moses came\" is: into the camp of Israel, and he told the people all the words of YHWH — the positive and negative commandments, which are written from \"You have seen\" (Exodus 20:19) through \"for it will be a snare to you\" (Exodus 23:33). <b>And all the ordinances.</b> Which he set before them — they are those mentioned in this section." "<b>And all the people answered.</b> As if they were one man."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:37:54.689012649Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}